        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: закон",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "закон (zakón) — \"a law\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Новый закон начнёт действовать в январе. Nóvyy zakón nachnyót déystvovat v yanvaré. The new law will come into force in January."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. По закону — by law."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "закон (zakón) is inherited from Proto-Slavic zakonŭ (EtymDB), built from за- and кон, an old word for a limit or a starting line that is still heard in испокон веков \"from time immemorial\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
